+# Documentation Bucket Configuration Guide
+
+## 🚨 Current Status
+
+The old bucket configuration has been **REMOVED** and needs to be configured with your new bucket details.
+
+## 📋 Quick Setup Steps
+
+### Step 1: Configure Your Bucket Details
+
+You have **two options** for configuration:
+
+#### Option A: Configure in `.env` (Recommended)
+
+Edit `/home/will/Projects/haive/.env` and fill in the TODO values:
+
+```bash
+# Cloudflare R2 Configuration
+CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id
+CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-api-token
+CLOUDFLARE_R2_ENDPOINT=https://your-account-id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
+CLOUDFLARE_R2_BUCKET=your-bucket-name
+
+# AWS CLI compatible settings for R2
+AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-r2-access-key
+AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-secret-key
+AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=https://your-account-id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
+AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=auto
+```
+
+#### Option B: Use Interactive Setup
+
+```bash
+cd /home/will/Projects/haive/scripts/r2_upload
+./setup.sh
+```
+
+### Step 2: Get Your R2 Credentials
+
+1. Go to [Cloudflare Dashboard](https://dash.cloudflare.com)
+2. Navigate to R2 → Overview
+3. Click "Manage R2 API Tokens"
+4. Create a new API token with:
+   - Permissions: Object Read & Write
+   - Specify bucket: Your bucket name
+   - TTL: No expiry (or as needed)
+5. Copy the Access Key ID and Secret Access Key
+
+### Step 3: Create Your R2 Bucket (if needed)
+
+1. In Cloudflare Dashboard → R2
+2. Click "Create bucket"
+3. Name it (e.g., `haive-docs`)
+4. Choose a region
+5. After creation, go to Settings → Custom Domains
+6. Add a custom domain for public access (optional)
+
+### Step 4: Test Configuration
+
+```bash
+# Test that configuration is valid
+cd /home/will/Projects/haive/scripts/r2_upload
+source ./config.sh  # Should not show errors if configured
+
+# Build documentation first
+cd /home/will/Projects/haive
+./scripts/build_all_docs.sh
+
+# Upload to your bucket
+./scripts/r2_upload/upload_all.sh
+```
+
+## 📁 File Structure
+
+- **Configuration Files:**
+  - `/home/will/Projects/haive/.env` - Environment variables (credentials)
+  - `/home/will/Projects/haive/scripts/r2_upload/config.sh` - Bucket configuration
+
+- **Upload Scripts:**
+  - `upload_all.sh` - Basic upload without deletion
+  - `simple_upload.sh` - Upload with `--delete` flag
+  - `upload_with_navigation.sh` - Upload with navigation injection
+
+- **Helper Files:**
+  - `setup.sh` - Interactive configuration wizard
+  - `README.md` - Detailed documentation
+
+## 🔧 Configuration Options
+
+### For Cloudflare R2:
+
+```bash
+STORAGE_TYPE="r2"
+R2_ACCOUNT_ID="your-account-id"
+R2_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+R2_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-custom-domain.com"  # Or https://pub-xxx.r2.dev
+```
+
+### For AWS S3:
+
+```bash
+STORAGE_TYPE="s3"
+S3_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+S3_REGION="us-east-1"
+S3_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com"
+```
+
+## 🚀 Public Access Setup
+
+### For R2:
+
+1. Go to your bucket settings in Cloudflare
+2. Either:
+   - Enable public access (generates pub-xxx.r2.dev URL)
+   - Add a custom domain for branded URLs
+
+### For S3:
+
+1. Configure bucket policy for public read access
+2. Or use CloudFront distribution for CDN
+
+## 📝 Notes
+
+- All scripts validate configuration before running
+- Scripts will fail with clear error messages if configuration is incomplete
+- The `.env` file is gitignored for security
+- Use `.env.example` as a template
+
+## 🆘 Troubleshooting
+
+### "R2 configuration is incomplete!"
+
+- Edit `.env` or `config.sh` with your bucket details
+- Run `./setup.sh` for interactive configuration
+
+### "AWS credentials not found!"
+
+- Add AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY to `.env`
+
+### "Access Denied" errors
+
+- Check that your API token has Object Read & Write permissions
+- Verify the bucket name is correct
+- Ensure the token is for the correct bucket
+
+## 📚 Documentation URLs
+
+After successful upload, your documentation will be available at:
+
+- Main docs: `{PUBLIC_URL}/`
+- Package docs: `{PUBLIC_URL}/packages/{package-name}/`
+
+Example structure:
+
+```
+https://your-domain.com/
+├── index.html (main docs)
+└── packages/
+    ├── haive-core/
+    ├── haive-agents/
+    ├── haive-tools/
+    ├── haive-mcp/
+    ├── haive-games/
+    ├── haive-dataflow/
+    ├── haive-prebuilt/
+    └── haive-hap/
+```
