+# Documentation Upload Scripts
+
+This directory contains scripts for uploading Haive documentation to cloud storage (Cloudflare R2 or AWS S3).
+
+## ⚠️ Initial Setup Required
+
+The bucket configuration has been cleared and needs to be set up before use.
+
+## Configuration
+
+All bucket configuration is centralized in `config.sh`. To set up your deployment target:
+
+### Option 1: Use Cloudflare R2 (Current Default)
+
+Edit `config.sh` and update:
+
+```bash
+STORAGE_TYPE="r2"
+R2_ACCOUNT_ID="your-account-id"
+R2_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+R2_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-public-url.r2.dev"
+```
+
+### Option 2: Use AWS S3
+
+Edit `config.sh` and update:
+
+```bash
+STORAGE_TYPE="s3"
+S3_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+S3_REGION="us-east-1"
+S3_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com"
+```
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+The scripts expect AWS credentials in `/home/will/Projects/haive/.env`:
+
+```bash
+AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-access-key
+AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret-key
+```
+
+For Cloudflare R2, use the R2 API tokens as AWS credentials.
+
+## Available Scripts
+
+### 1. `upload_all.sh`
+
+Basic upload of all documentation without deletion of existing files.
+
+```bash
+./upload_all.sh
+```
+
+### 2. `simple_upload.sh`
+
+Upload with `--delete` flag to remove files not in source.
+
+```bash
+./simple_upload.sh
+```
+
+### 3. `upload_with_navigation.sh`
+
+Upload with injected navigation enhancements (requires `inject_navigation.py`).
+
+```bash
+./upload_with_navigation.sh
+```
+
+## Quick Setup Guide
+
+### Step 1: Configure Your Bucket
+
+Edit `config.sh` and fill in the TODO sections:
+
+```bash
+# For R2:
+R2_ACCOUNT_ID="your-account-id"
+R2_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+R2_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-url.r2.dev"
+
+# OR for S3:
+STORAGE_TYPE="s3"
+S3_BUCKET="your-bucket-name"
+S3_REGION="us-east-1"
+S3_PUBLIC_URL="https://your-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com"
+```
+
+### Step 2: Set Up Credentials
+
+1. Copy the template: `cp /home/will/Projects/haive/.env.template /home/will/Projects/haive/.env`
+2. Edit `.env` with your actual AWS/R2 credentials
+
+### Step 3: Run Upload
+
+```bash
+# Build docs first
+cd /home/will/Projects/haive
+./scripts/build_all_docs.sh
+
+# Then upload
+./scripts/r2_upload/upload_all.sh
+```
+
+## Changing Buckets
+
+To change to a new bucket:
+
+1. Edit `config.sh` with new bucket details
+2. Update credentials in `.env` if needed
+3. Run any of the upload scripts
+
+The scripts will automatically use the new configuration.
+
+## Package List
+
+The following packages are included in uploads:
+
+- haive-core
+- haive-agents
+- haive-tools
+- haive-mcp
+- haive-games
+- haive-dataflow
+- haive-prebuilt
+- haive-hap
+
+To add or remove packages, edit the `PACKAGES` variable in `config.sh`.
+
+## URLs Structure
+
+Documentation is organized as:
+
+- Main docs: `{PUBLIC_URL}/`
+- Package docs: `{PUBLIC_URL}/packages/{package-name}/`
+
+Example with current R2 setup:
+
+- Main: https://pub-7f716b302a2948e19f08b49b71408039.r2.dev/
